@nicolas-grekas  Thanks for the feedback!

The main motivation for this change is to avoid opening a separate TCP connection for each tube. With the current approach, each transport is configured with a single tube, so using multiple tubes means creating multiple transports and, consequently, multiple connections. I'd like to reuse a single connection to send messages to different tubes.

Additionally, although tube names can be known in advance, in some cases the target tube is determined at runtime, based on the message or application logic.

This is why I'd prefer to support selecting the target tube per message rather than requiring a separate transport for each tube.

